PUBLIC RESPONSE: {B1}  
I agree with the majority: W B1 is the unique kill-initiating move. First, W B2 is self-atari—B2 has only B1 as a liberty, so Black B1 immediately captures it. Even if White later tries to salvage with A4, Black can answer A3 and create a seki around A1/B2, so Black lives.  

The B1 line is forced: W B1 puts C1–C2 in atari, so Black must play B B2. Then W A4 reduces Black to liberties A1 and A3. If Black plays A1, W A3 leaves the whole Black group with only B1, which Black cannot fill; White captures next. If Black plays A3, W A1 captures immediately. Thus the only move that initiates a kill sequence is B1.

